    "If Statements"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c1816dbe-8c24-4115-b08d-2af166140bb5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If statements and conditionals let your code make decisions.\n",
    "\n",
    "If a condition is true, run this part of code.\n",
    "\n",
    "If it is false, run a different part of code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "bbd16e73-3c03-48fc-80cb-b87d1631d72e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "It's hot!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# example with numbers:\n",
    "\n",
    "temperature = 90\n",
    "\n",
    "if temperature > 80:\n",
    "    print(\"It's hot!\")\n",
    "elif temperature >= 60:\n",
    "    print(\"It's nice.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"It's cold.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6b96bea4-55fb-49b0-b573-a2436f0f594b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "if condition:\n",
    "    # code if this condition is true will run\n",
    "    # second line i want to run. must be indented\n",
    "elif another_condition:\n",
    "    # code if first condition is false, and this other condition is true will run\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # code if none of the above are true"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aed4c449-b56b-45d0-b3b3-da266a67fa8b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "if condition:\n",
    "    if another_condition:\n",
    "        # code will run if BOTH if statements are true.\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # code will run if first if statement is not true"
   ]
  },
